// Package watch is the per-library filesystem-change scan trigger (the
// watch-scan design): it watches every library root for filesystem events
// and fires Deps.Scan for a library once its root has sat still for the
// debounce quiet window — coalescing a burst of writes into one scan —
// while a periodic reconcile walk backstops the event stream (missed
// events, roots changed while the server was down, libraries with no
// events at all all converge within one ReconcileInterval).
//
// The package is a pure leaf (D1, the internal/browse precedent): it
// imports NOTHING from mellifera. The library set and the scan action
// arrive as cmd-built Deps closures, so the dependency direction stays
// DOWN — cmd → watch wiring only; api, scan, and store are untouched.
//
// The trigger policy is a pure state machine over an explicit now (D3):
// per library, observe extends the quiet-window deadline on a filesystem
// event (or marks the library dirty when its scan is already running),
// dueFires reports the window's expiry and arms the scan, and completed
// clears the run — re-arming one trailing scan when the run failed or
// events arrived mid-run, so a change made during a scan still converges.
// All timing decisions run on injected times (deterministic tests, the
// TestUrgentLanePreferred lesson); the fsnotify adapter (task 1.2) is the
// thin shell that feeds the engine real events and real scans.
package watch
